  "In Duncker’s radiation problem, the solution is to send **several low-intensity rays converging on the tumor from different directions at the same time**. Each path through the surrounding tissue receives only a low intensity, while the combined intensity at the tumor is enough to destroy it. Only about 10 percent of participants reach this without the helpful analogy."
