  "A fortress and a tumor do not look alike, so focusing on that difference can keep a person from noticing that both tasks need a strong combined effect at a central target while the separate approaches stay safe. Making the surface features more similar makes the shared relationship easier to notice, because noticing finds a possible source and mapping works out how it corresponds to the target."
